  "marked": "^14.1.0"

package-lock.json:
  "node_modules/marked": {
    "version": "14.1.2",
    "resolved": "https://registry.npmjs.org/marked/-/marked-14.1.2.tgz",
    "integrity": "sha512-FAKE...=="
  }

Registry snapshot (npm view marked versions):
  [ ..., "14.1.2", "14.1.3", "15.0.0" ]

The CI build job runs: npm ci

Statement: "CI installs marked 14.1.2, although 14.1.3 also satisfies ^14.1.0."', 'single_choice'::question_type, 'True. npm ci installs exactly the versions in the lockfile and never resolves ranges again; it only uses package.json to check that the two files agree, and 14.1.2 satisfies ^14.1.0, so they do. 14.1.3 arrives only when someone runs npm install or npm update on purpose and commits the new lockfile. Even npm install would keep 14.1.2 here, because the locked version still satisfies the range. The misconception is that a caret range floats to the newest match on every install; with a committed lockfile, the range only matters when the lockfile changes.', 1, 5
    WHERE NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM challenge.questions WHERE challenge_id = (SELECT id FROM challenge.challenges WHERE public_id = 'chal_quiz_ssc_121') AND order_index = 1)
