Statement: "The checker trusted a scope that nobody at CodeDev owns, because "@codedev-ui/form-utils".startsWith("@codedev") is true."', 'single_choice'::question_type, 'True. startsWith compares characters, not scopes: "@codedev-ui", "@codedevs" and "@codedev.ui" all start with "@codedev". The scope of a scoped name is the text up to the first "/", and it must be compared as a whole string with the owned list. This is the root cause; the regex that silently drops other scoped names is the second bug in the same loop. The common mistake is to treat a prefix as ownership: on a public registry anyone can register any scope name nobody has taken yet, including one that looks like yours.', 3, 5
