Statement: "Because the package is published under the @codedev scope, it comes from the CodeDev team and the publisher check can be skipped."', 'single_choice'::question_type, 'False. A scope belongs to whoever registered it on that registry. Here the team''s packages use @codedev-internal from a private registry; @codedev is not mapped in .npmrc, so it resolves from the public registry, where it has a maintainer nobody knows, an age of a few days and no repository. A familiar-looking scope is a lure, not an identity: check who owns the scope and that .npmrc maps it, as in lessons 2.1 and 3.3. The misconception is that the scope name proves the publisher.', 2, 5
